---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-discussion</code> is the conversation on a record, such as a
  ticket, an order or a document. It holds
  <code>wc-discussion-comment</code> and
  <code>wc-discussion-activity</code> elements and a
  <code>wc-comment-composer</code> under them. Comments are Markdown, with
  mentions, one level of replies, and inline reply and edit.
</p>
<p>
  The app owns the data. The discussion fires events and changes nothing; the
  app adds, updates or removes the elements, usually after saving to its
  server. Every event bubbles, so one set of listeners on the discussion is
  enough:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <code>submit</code> (cancelable): <code>{'{ value, mentions, parentId }'}</code>,
    a new comment (<code>parentId</code> null) or a reply. Cancel it to keep
    the text in the composer, for example while a save fails.
  </li>
  <li>
    <code>edit</code> (cancelable): <code>{'{ commentId, value, mentions }'}</code>
    when someone saves an edit.
  </li>
  <li><code>delete</code>, <code>reply</code> and <code>copy-link</code>.</li>
  <li>
    <code>search</code>: answer it by setting <code>suggestions</code> on the
    discussion.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  Try it: add a comment, reply, mention someone with <code>@</code>, or edit
  and delete your own comments from their menu.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-discussion id="discussion-usage" style="display:block; width:100%; max-width: 44rem;">
    <wc-discussion-activity
      icon="add_circle"
      author="Ana Lima"
      datetime="2026-11-07T08:12:00Z"
      value="opened the ticket"
    ></wc-discussion-activity>
    <wc-discussion-comment
      comment-id="c1"
      author="Ravi Kumar"
      datetime="2026-11-07T08:40:00Z"
      href="#c1"
      value="I can reproduce it on **staging**. The export job stops after 500 rows:"
    >
      <wc-discussion-comment
        slot="replies"
        comment-id="c2"
        author="Ana Lima"
        datetime="2026-11-07T09:05:00Z"
        value="Thanks [@Ravi Kumar](mention:usr_7). Same on production."
      ></wc-discussion-comment>
    </wc-discussion-comment>
    <wc-discussion-activity
      icon="swap_horiz"
      author="Ravi Kumar"
      datetime="2026-11-07T09:20:00Z"
      value="changed **State** from New to In progress"
    ></wc-discussion-activity>
  </wc-discussion>
  <script is:inline src="/assets/js/discussion-demo.js"></script>
  <script is:inline>
    window.peacockDiscussionDemo(document.getElementById('discussion-usage'));
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3 class="text-title-medium">Your own composer</h3>

<p>
  Put a <code>wc-comment-composer</code> in the <code>composer</code> slot to
  add an avatar or footer controls, such as a choice between a public comment
  and an internal work note. The <code>header</code> slot sits above the
  entries.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-discussion id="discussion-custom" style="display:block; width:100%; max-width: 44rem;">
    <div slot="header" class="text-title-medium">Activity</div>
    <wc-discussion-comment
      comment-id="w1"
      author="Mei Chen"
      datetime="2026-11-06T16:00:00Z"
      value="Rolled back the config change."
    >
      <wc-tag slot="badge" intent="warning">Work note</wc-tag>
    </wc-discussion-comment>
    <wc-comment-composer slot="composer" placeholder="Add a comment or work note">
      <wc-avatar slot="avatar" name="You" size="md"></wc-avatar>
      <wc-select slot="start" id="discussion-visibility" size="sm" value="comment" aria-label="Visibility">
        <wc-option value="comment">Comment</wc-option>
        <wc-option value="work">Work note</wc-option>
      </wc-select>
    </wc-comment-composer>
  </wc-discussion>
  <script is:inline>
    const visibility = document.getElementById('discussion-visibility');
    window.peacockDiscussionDemo(document.getElementById('discussion-custom'), {
      badge: () => (visibility.value === 'work' ? 'Work note' : ''),
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
